<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guayaquil</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guayaquil is the largest city and main port of Ecuador, on the Guayas river near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-guayaquil">Gulf of Guayaquil</a>. Founded by the Spanish in the 1530s, it became the chief port and shipyard of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/audiencia">Audiencia</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a>. It declared independence on 9 October 1820, was annexed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> in 1822, and hosted his meeting with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guayaquil.jpg" alt="Guayaquil" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Padaguan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Faro_de_Guayaquil.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
